+### ISSUE: SPEC_GAP (PASS 1)
+
+`scripts/compound-v-emit-preflight.py:279-280` — the comment inside the **emitted JavaScript
+template**, which reaches every generated pre-flight script:
+
+```
+// writes exactly one document. Bash is admitted only for the recall query,
+// through a clamp, because dogfood 24 proved it is denied without one.
+```
+
+Confirmed live in the script I emitted (`cv-pf-probe.js:147-148`), three lines above
+`bashCommandClamp: CFG.clamp`, whose value in that same file is five rules, three of them git.
+The design doc's amendment 2 is *"The singularity claims go"*; 1A's `grep -n 'ONE exception\|one
+shell form'` pattern found only two of the three instances, so the spec named two, the plan named
+two, and the implementer edited two. The gap originates upstream — the implementer executed the plan
+faithfully — but the artifact still ships a false statement about the size of its own Bash surface,
+in the file this job owns, at the exact place a reader checks it.
+
+→ Rewrite `:279-280` to name the recall query **and** read-only git history, same as `:48-49` and
+`:206-207`. Do not add the deleted `dogfood 24` clause to the git half — that provenance belongs to
+the recall query only.
+
+### ISSUE: CONSTRAINT_VIOLATION (PASS 1) — library-audit §7 constraint 2
+
+`scripts/compound-v-emit-preflight.py:215-217`:
+
+```
+# Read-only git history for the auditors (v3.4.13, finding 145): 1A's
+# "recent commits" evidence comes from git, not from dated prose. Only
+# these three forms — nothing that can touch the tree or the index.
+```
+
+`docs/superpowers/library-audit/2026-09-03-v3-4-13-preflight-git-history.md:163-167` says:
+**MUST NOT** *"describe `git log`/`git show` as unconditionally 'read-only' or as guaranteeing
+'nothing that can change the tree or the index' without qualifying that this is true only of git's
+own object database — both commands carry a live, verified `--output=<file>` option that writes
+arbitrary content to any filesystem path the process can reach."* The comment lands on the
+prohibited phrasing almost word for word, unqualified, with no pointer to the acceptance in the
+design doc's amendment 4.
+
+The design doc satisfies §7-3 (the risk is recorded); the **code** does not satisfy §7-2 (the
+qualification does not travel with the claim). This text was mandated verbatim by the plan's Step 1
+code block, so the defect is inherited, not invented — it is still unsatisfied at the seam where the
+audit binds, and it is one clause from being right.
+
+→ Qualify in place: `git log`/`git show` are read-only *with respect to git's object database*;
+`--output=<file>` remains reachable and is accepted per the design doc's amendment 4. Cite the
+amendment so the next reader finds the acceptance instead of re-deriving the risk.
