+## QUALITY
+
+Run after SPEC because spec drift is judged first; the two SPEC findings are comment-scope and do
+not obstruct a quality read of the same diff. **Clean — no issue found.**
+
+**2.1 Code quality.** The two new locals are correct and fail-closed. `_py_rules` at `:506` is
+defined negatively (`not r.startswith("Bash(git ")`), so a hypothetical future non-python,
+non-git rule — `Bash(rg:*)` — falls *into* `_py_rules`, fails the `" -B " in r` assertion, and
+breaks the build. That is the right direction. Likewise `:507-511` admits only
+`compound-v-memory.py` substrings or exact members of `_GIT_FORMS`; anything else fails. Nit, not an
+issue: the name `_py_rules` describes an intent the predicate does not literally implement
+("non-git" ≠ "python"); the mismatch is benign precisely because it errs strict, and the name came
+from the plan.
+
+**2.2 No regression.** No check was deleted. Extracted the pre-change file at
+`086543dd^` and diffed the `check("…")` name lists:
+
+```
+2c2  < "Bash is clamped to the recall query, not denied outright"
+     > "Bash is clamped to the recall query plus read-only git history, not denied outright"
+21a22 > "no git form beyond log/blame/show can slip into the clamp"
+28a30 > "the clamp admits git log/blame/show for the auditors"
+```
+
+One renamed, two added, **zero removed**. Selftest total moved 38 → 40 and every one passes. No
+other module imports `build_plan`/`emit_script` (1A §8 grepped it; re-confirmed — the only
+repo-wide referencer of this script outside `scripts/` is `skills/compound-v/SKILL.md`, which makes
